\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Chirality and the volume element}
\date{2026-11-13}

\p{Where the product of the represented generators is the volume
element, that product is #{\psI}. A grading that is not the
volume element is #{(-1)^{\deg}}. Mathematical physics writes
#{C=i^m\Gamma_1\cdots\Gamma_{2m}}, or #{\gamma_5} up to a phase.
Geometric calculus writes the pseudoscalar. The phase #{\ui^m}
in \ref{fdip-009X} is the one for which the square is the
identity in the Euclidean signature of the [covariant centered differences](fdip-009O).}
